# Staphylococcus aureus, the five locus MLVA of Sabat et al. 2003, read as a band pattern on an
# agarose gel. The loci are in the order of Table 2. The paper defines no profile string, so this
# order is a presentation choice; see scheme.yml.
#
# Primers are Table 2 as published. The sspA pair carries IUPAC ambiguity codes, M and Y, which
# is why that marker is found by the rescue pass rather than at word size 11.
#
# sdr is one primer pair that amplifies the tandemly arrayed sdrC, sdrD and sdrE genes together,
# by design, so it gives more than one product and is declared in known_multiple. In NCTC 8325 it
# gives two, 640 bp and 796 bp, from adjacent positions in that array.
#
# The search window is derived, not published: it allows thirty repeats either side of the product
# measured in NCTC 8325, and for sdr it spans both of that strain's products widened the same way.

clfA	GATTCTGACCCAGGTTCAGA	CTGTATCTGGTAATGGTTCTTT	457-1537
clfB	ATGGTGATTCAGCAGTAAATCC	CATTATTTGGTGGTGTAACTCTT	288-1368
sdr	GTAACAATTACGGATCATGATG	TACCTGTTTCTGGTAATGCTTT	100-1336
spa	AGCACCAAAAGAGGAAGACAA	GTTTAACGACATGTACTCCGT	60-1028
ssp	ATCMATTTYGCMAAYGATGACCA	TTGTCTGAATTATTGTTATCGCC	60-425
